{"chunk_id": "8aea1f61b5de", "text": "As Rama prepares to depart for exile, the palace is overwhelmed with grief. After respectfully taking leave of his father Dasaratha and the queens, Rama, Sita, and Lakshmana mount the chariot prepared by the charioteer Sumantra. Sumitra blesses Lakshmana, urging him to serve Rama with absolute devotion and to regard the forest as Ayodhya itself. When the chariot sets out for the Dandaka forest, the entire city erupts in sorrow\u2014men, women, soldiers, and animals follow behind, weeping and pleading for the chariot to slow so they may see Rama\u2019s face. King Dasaratha himself runs barefoot after it. Torn between the king\u2019s command to stop and Rama\u2019s command to go faster, Sumantra finally drives on as Rama, bound by duty, turns away from his grieving parents.\nRama, Sita, and Lakshmana depart Ayodhya in a chariot as the grieving city, royal family, and citizens run after them in anguish.\nThemes: exile and duty, filial devotion, public grief, loyalty of Lakshmana and Sita, conflict between love and dharma", "vector": [0.0198860764503479, -0.01093869749456644, -0.01793539896607399, -0.011609242297708988, -0.029585281386971474, 0.033215709030628204, -0.025534914806485176, 0.0007810331298969686, -0.02075304463505745, -0.022283785045146942, 0.016878781840205193, 0.01747482270002365, 0.0021606467198580503, 0.02764814905822277, 0.00048258958850055933, -0.0029175502713769674, 0.03909483551979065, -0.008236194960772991, 0.034434881061315536, 0.006041682790964842, 0.003840397112071514, -0.015036474913358688, 0.005838487297296524, 0.00971275009214878, -0.011859850026667118, -0.007416639942675829, 0.01943904720246792, -0.028095180168747902, 0.016743319109082222, -0.020847870036959648, -0.004131644032895565, -0.01679750345647335, -0.0038200775161385536, -0.02311011403799057, -0.028907962143421173, 0.004507556091994047, -0.0066512697376310825, -0.0026991150807589293, 0.01752900891005993, -0.008324246853590012, 0.0031105861999094